    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="15" relname="span">I have experienced these things as well.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="1" relname="elaboration">This is especially true when visiting secure websites.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="4" relname="concession">You can click on a button,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="13" relname="span">but it may not prompt anything to happen.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="11" relname="span">This can cause nothing to happen or even worse duplication.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="14" relname="span">With purchasing items online or online banking this can be a big hassle.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="8" relname="nonvolitional-cause">If you get charged twice for something or you transfer double the amount that you wanted to,</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="12" relname="span">it can be a long drawn out process to get those funds back.</segment>
        <group id="9" type="span"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="9" relname="span"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="6" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="5" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="11" relname="nonvolitional-result"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="10" relname="background"/>
    </body>
